{"query":"There is a scam involving Santander customers being sent fake bank cards. evidence","results":[{"date":"Feb 18, 2021","position":1,"site_name":"fullfact.org","snippet":"We can’t find any evidence that this scam exists. Posts warning people about a possible scam involving Santander bank cards have been shared tens of thousands of times on Facebook. The posts largely use the same text, which was being shared at least as early as October 2020.","title":"Santander bank card ‘scam’ probably doesn’t exist – Full Fact","url":"https://fullfact.org/online/santander-card-scam/"},{"date":"Aug 30, 2026","position":2,"site_name":"www.theguardian.com","snippet":"Meanwhile, Santander says more than £3m has been stolen from its customers through bank impersonation scams so far this year, with an average loss of £6,000. Because the messages are being...","title":"New payment set up? Get in touch! The bank scam where your ...","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/money/2026/aug/30/new-payment-set-up-get-in-touch-the-bank-scam-where-your-bank-is-the-scammer"},{"date":"Feb 12, 2025","position":3,"site_name":"fallriverreporter.com","snippet":"A Massachusetts police department is warning the public of a new scam that has already left victims. The Barnstable Police Department have announced that victims are being contacted by their “Santander Bank Fraud Department” via a text message.","title":"Massachusetts police issue warning to public after residents ...","url":"https://fallriverreporter.com/massachusetts-police-issue-warning-to-public-after-residents-victimized-in-new-scam-that-resulted-in-withdrawals-from-bank-account/"},{"position":4,"site_name":"www.santanderbank.com","snippet":"Protect yourself from fraud with Santander Bank security tools. Discover how to report scams, set alerts, lock your card, and keep your accounts secure.","title":"What You Can Do to Protect Your Information | Santander Bank","url":"https://www.santanderbank.com/personal/security-center/what-you-can-do-to-prevent-fraud"},{"date":"Mar 1, 2023","position":5,"site_name":"www.express.co.uk","snippet":"A Santander customer warned others about a highly convincing scam where the fraudsters knew his card details.","title":"Santander issues advice after ‘realistic’ scam email included ...","url":"https://www.express.co.uk/finance/personalfinance/1740974/Santander-scam-warning-banking-fraud"},{"date":"Sep 18, 2026","position":6,"site_name":"www.bitdefender.com","snippet":"Portugal’s National Republican Guard (GNR) recently warned about a new scam that begins with an unsolicited bank card delivered to someone’s home. The card can be followed by a phone call, text message or email from a person claiming to represent a bank or financial institution.","title":"Unexpected Bank Card in the Mail? It Might Be a Scam","url":"https://www.bitdefender.com/en-us/blog/hotforsecurity/unexpected-bank-card-in-the-mail-scam"},{"position":7,"site_name":"www.santander.co.uk","snippet":"Criminals use DocuSign to send documents for payment redirection scams, or to download malware to your device. The email address they’re sending from looks like the real DocuSign one, but the document inside is fake.","title":"Latest fraud updates - Santander UK","url":"https://www.santander.co.uk/personal/support/fraud-and-security/fraud-updates"}],"total_results":7,"page":0}